## File: `/home/dmdevelo/Desktop/dmdevelon_projects/DMDevelon/components/chat/MessageBubble.jsx`

### 1. URL Regex Pattern (Lines 47-48)

```js
const URL_RE =
  /(https?:\/\/[^\s<>"{}|\\^`[\]]+?)(?=[.,;:!?]*(?:\s|$)|[.,;:!?]*$)/g;
```

This regex:
- Matches `http://` or `https://` followed by any non-whitespace, non-special-character sequence.
- Uses a **positive lookahead** `(?=[.,;:!?]*(?:\s|$)|[.,;:!?]*$)` to **exclude trailing punctuation** (`.`, `,`, `;`, `:`, `!`, `?`) from the captured URL, so `"Check https://example.com."` doesn't include the period in the link.

### 2. `renderBodyWithLinks` Function (Lines 50-73)

```js
function renderBodyWithLinks(text) {
  if (!text) return text;
  const parts = [];
  let last = 0;
  for (const match of text.matchAll(URL_RE)) {
    if (match.index > last) parts.push(text.slice(last, match.index));
    parts.push(
      <a
        key={match.index}
        href={match[1]}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        className="underline"
        style={{ color: "#0f2f57" }}
      >
        {match[1]}
      </a>,
    );
    last = match.index + match[1].length;
  }
  if (last < text.length) parts.push(text.slice(last));
  return parts.length <= 1 ? text : parts;
}
```

This function:
1. Returns the raw text if it's falsy.
2. Iterates over all URL matches using `text.matchAll(URL_RE)`.
3. Pushes plain-text segments (non-URL text) and `<a>` elements (for matched URLs) into a `parts` array, interleaving them in order.
4. Each `<a>` tag has `target="_blank"`, `rel="noopener noreferrer"`, `className="underline"`, and a fixed dark-blue color (`#0f2f57`).
5. If no URLs were found (`parts.length <= 1`), it returns the plain text as-is (no array wrapping).

### 3. Rendering Usage (Lines 225-227)

```jsx
{message.body && (
  <p className="text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">
    {renderBodyWithLinks(message.body)}
  </p>
)}
```

The message body is rendered inside a `<p>` tag with `whitespace-pre-wrap` (preserves newlines) and `break-words` (prevents overflow on long unbroken strings). The output of `renderBodyWithLinks` is rendered as the children of this `<p>`.

---

### Potential Issues

The logic looks correct at first glance — the regex should match standard URLs and the function produces proper `<a>` elements. If URLs are appearing as plain text, possible causes include:

1. **The URL format doesn't match the regex** — e.g., URLs without a scheme (`example.com` vs `https://example.com`), or URLs containing characters excluded by the character class like `<>"{}|\\^`[\]]`.
2. **The `parts.length <= 1` early return** — If `matchAll` finds a match but something goes wrong (e.g., the match object is somehow not advancing `last`), it could fall through to returning raw text.
3. **The regex lookahead** — The lookahead `(?=[.,;:!?]*(?:\s|$)|[.,;:!?]*$)` requires the URL to be followed by whitespace, end-of-string, or trailing punctuation then end/whitespace. A URL that ends mid-string followed immediately by another word (e.g., `https://example.comfoo`) would NOT match because the lookahead would fail.

